@startuml CryptoWeb-E3-mvc-conditionalorders
title CryptoWeb - Conditional Orders and Scheduled Execution (MVC view)

!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 75
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
hide circle


package "React view and API adapter" {
  class "Trades" as TV <<React view>> {
    +Trades()
  }
  class "tradeApi" as TA <<API object>> {
    +cancelOrder()
    +getOpenOrders()
  }
}

package "Controllers / asynchronous execution" {
  class "Order Controller" as OC <<controller module>> {
    +postorder()
    +getorders()
    +updateorder()
    +deleteorder()
  }
  class "Order Executor" as OE <<scheduled job module>> {
    +shouldExecute()
    +markExecuted()
    +markFailed()
  }
  class "Live Price Service" as LP <<service module>> {
    +getPrice()
  }
  class "Core Gateway" as GW <<gateway module>> {
    +executeInternalTrade()
  }
}

package "Mongoose models" {
  class "Order" as O <<Mongoose model>> {
    +userId
    +symbol
    +side
    +orderType
    +qty
    +price
    +status
  }
  class "Trade" as T <<Mongoose model>> {
    +orderId : ObjectId [optional]
    +price : String
    +fillId : Number
  }
}

TV ..> TA : submits
TA ..> OC : REST
OC ..> O : create/cancel
OE ..> O : polls/claims
OE ..> LP : reads live price
OE ..> GW : Core settlement
OE ..> T : saves executed trade
T "0..*" --> "0..1" O : orderId

legend bottom
Conditional order requests use tradeApi in the implemented Trades React page.
An executed order can produce a trade; market trades have no Order document.
endlegend

@enduml
